cl emits object-file symbols here that cxx1 does not, or the other way round, for reasons that are codegen and not naming: a deleting destructor cl writes and cxx1 emits only where a vtable needs one, and the exception funclets this target's handlers are built from. The mangled names both compilers do emit agree; tests/names.sh checks those against clang on all three targets. Recorded rather than argued with until somebody has a reason to make the two objects identical.
